  "_approach": "Clap/snare-roll build in two bars: bar 1 keeps the 4/4 kick with the clap on a loose 8th roll; bar 2 drops the kick and accelerates the clap into 16ths then a 32nd-note roll with the snare joining for the final push, velocity climbing to 127 on the last 32nd so the drop's downbeat lands hardest. This is techno's version of the drop-cue snare roll — shorter and less frantic than a hard techno wall, since techno rolls build over one bar, not four.",
